# Native async fn in traits

**This feature is unstable and is only available in nightly.**

`async fn` can now be declared in traits, and can be implemented in ad-hoc impls, as well as in `impl Trait` blocks. This allows for more ergonomic APIs, as the return type can be inferred in many cases, and the `async fn` can be called without a `Trait::method()` syntax.


    #![feature(async_fn_in_traits)]

    trait Trait {
        async fn method();
    }

    impl Trait for i32 {
        async fn method() {}
    }

    async fn call_method<T: Trait>(t: T) {
        t.method().await;
    }

    call_method(1).await;

