# Module System and Keywords

## `self` is a valid identifier in modules

In the 2018 edition, `self` is a valid identifier in module paths, allowing you to refer to the current module from within. This is similar to how `self` is used in trait implementations.


    mod foo {
        pub mod bar {
            // In the 2015 edition, this would fail to compile.
            // In the 2018 edition, this works!
            pub fn call_self() {
                // The path to the current module, `foo::bar`.
                self::call_super();

                // The path to the parent module, `foo`.
                super::call_parent();
            }
        }
    }

    fn main() {
        foo::bar::call_self();
    }

